+| Broad E1 treated as exempt from growth-channel risk | Author's preference preserved; independent coverage and effective-control condition applies on every branch | Noncompetitive hazardous growth is a counterexample to the exemption; real-world C1 remains unmeasured |
+| Safe withdrawal assumed decisive capability was never built | Separate pre-construction and post-construction states, candidate disposition, executor and knowledge limits | Later fallback remains a C4 design question until specified measures work before protected loss; no automatic reversibility advantage |
+| Finite sprint rebutted as though every freeze were a monopoly | Relinquishing superiority and enforcing it are compared separately | Peak exposure and commitment objections remain; imposed unequal incidence is conditional on monopoly enforcement |
+| Verified agreement allowed only as a bridge | Durable verified containment admitted if enforcement, independent correction and coverage conditions remain satisfied | A fixed enforcement witness establishes logical availability, not practical feasibility |
+| d* treated as hazard coverage and a sufficient funding formula | Institutional-independence resources separated from technical coverage and effective response | Resource-to-performance production relation remains open in S13 and X10 |
+| Test D/G assigned unsupported predictions to Pierson and structural realism | Relabelled within-model/intervention predictions pending matched rival derivations | No claim to distinguish a literature without specifying its comparable model |
+| Zero tax allowed automatic withdrawal | Zero selects neither variant; persistence evidence required in summaries as in the main recommendation | RP retains an unsafe initial share under neutral selection |
+| X1 omitted the tax condition for a detection ceiling | Expected enforceable sanction compared jointly with the changing tax | A faster-falling tax can preserve deterrence |
+| Evaluation credited with producing context-dependent misalignment | EV6 attributes the intervention to safety training and evaluation to revealing or missing it | Experimental construction and unknown deployment prevalence remain explicit |
+| Benchmark and source shorthand | Dated benchmark gaps distinguished from persistent leads and sanctionability; source locators corrected | Public measures do not bound internal capability or the full response window |
+| Cognitive understanding treated as the only route | Functional dependence-counting separated from shared cognitive understanding | Local benefits and robust constraints can carry safeguards; shared understanding remains the author's proposed route to deliberate coordination |
